       "ImageDescription": {
        "value": "<i>The British Cotton Industry- Everyday Life at a British Cotton Mill, Lancashire, England, UK, 1945</i><br>\n<dl><dd>Cotton worker Lilian Alston fits cones of yarn into the V-shaped creel of the warping frame at a cotton mill, somewhere in Lancashire.  According to the original caption, this is the first stage in the job of weaving the yarn into cloth.  Rows and rows of reels can be seen on the frames behind her, as can a large wheeled basket full of yarn.</dd></dl>",
        "source": "commons-desc-page"
       },
